<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51464" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Xanthus</span></b> , i, m., =
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ξάνθος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>the name of several rivers.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A river of Troas</i>, confounded by many with the
			Scamander, <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 30, 33, § 124</span></i>; <i><span class="en">2, 103, 106, §
			230</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 1, 473</span></i>; <i><span class="en">5, 634
			al.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 2, 245</span></i>; <i><span class="en">9, 646</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Vitr. 8,
				3 <i>med.</i></span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A river in Lycia</i>, <i>near a town
				of the same name</i>, now <i>Essenide</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 1, 15,
				3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 4, 143</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">id. Cul. 14</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. C. 4,
				6, 26</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 27, 28, § 100</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">6, 34, 39, §
				214</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A small stream in Epirus</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 3,
				350</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
